BOOK REVIEW APP — ARCHITECTURE ASSUMPTIONS

Architecture: Three-Tier Azure Architecture

1. PRESENTATION / WEB TIER
Azure Service: Azure App Service
Purpose: Hosts the Book Review App frontend/presentation layer.
Network: Web subnet
Access: Receives traffic only from the public entry point.

2. APPLICATION / BUSINESS TIER
Azure Service: Azure Container Apps
Purpose: Runs the Book Review App backend/API.
Network: Application subnet
Access: Private/internal access only.
The backend is not directly exposed to the Internet.

3. DATABASE TIER
Azure Service: Azure Database for MySQL Flexible Server
Purpose: Stores Book Review App data.
Network: Database subnet / private access
Access: Only the application tier can connect to the database.

4. PUBLIC ENTRY POINT
Azure Service: Azure Application Gateway
Purpose: Single public entry point for users.
Security: WAF enabled.
Traffic: Internet → Application Gateway → Web Tier

5. NETWORK SECURITY
Azure Services: Virtual Network + NSGs + Private DNS
Purpose: Isolate the three tiers and enforce least-privilege traffic.

6. SECRET MANAGEMENT
Azure Service: Azure Key Vault
Purpose: Securely stores database credentials and application secrets.
Secrets are never stored directly in source code or exposed publicly.

7. MONITORING
Azure Service: Azure Monitor
Purpose: Collects metrics, logs, diagnostics, and alerts for important resources.

8. BACKUP & AVAILABILITY
Database backups and retention are enabled.
Availability settings are configured according to the selected Azure service capabilities.

TRAFFIC FLOW

Internet
   ↓
Application Gateway (Public)
   ↓
Web Tier
   ↓
Application Tier (Private)
   ↓
MySQL Database Tier (Private)

SECURITY PRINCIPLES

• Least-privilege network access
• No direct Internet access to application tier
• No direct Internet access to database tier
• Secrets stored in Key Vault
• Database accessed through private networking
• Monitoring and logging enabled